The indicator's
Network Health
is checked by reviewing the history of transitions between market regimes. A shift from the neutral (blue) zone to the Rough zone (red) signals that volatility has begun to behave explosively: upcoming price movements will be sharp, with rapid reversals. It is precisely under such conditions that trend-following systems incur the greatest losses.
A move into the blue zone is also very useful — it often coincides with a preceding trend reversal.
It remains to be seen how informative this feature is for machine learning models, but the screenshots give us hope that CatBoost or XGBoost models will learn to predict reversals more accurately than by chance, using our indicator.
